                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_351">London. Guildhall</orgName><p>BL Cotton Claudius D.ii fols. 1--24, 30--40, 42--115, 124--135,
                        266--277, Guildhall, 'Liber Custumarum', fols. v, 1--84, 86--102, 173--186,
                        and Oriel College 46, fols. 109--211, formed one volume. Fols. 16--39 of the
                        Corporation's 'Liber Albus' was originally part of this MS, but was removed
                        from it in the Middle Ages.</p><p>Fols. 109--199 formerly foliated 215--304;
                        fols. 200--208 formerly foliated as 362--370. Fol. 209 is blank. Fol. 210r
                        contains a medieval table of contents with folio nos. Fol. 211 is an
                        endleaf, formerly foliated 37[.] (the last digit torn off). The table of
                        contents covers Guildhall, 'Liber Custumarum' fols. 1--102, 173--186, and
                        Cotton Claudius D.ii fols. 1--24, 31--115, 124--135, 266--277, of which this
                        MS was once part.</p></provenance>
